    "url": "/projects/qbserve-blocker.html",
    "repo_url": "https://github.com/Avery2/Qbserve-Blocker",
    "body": "\n<p dir=\"auto\">I was unable to find an app that blocks apps based on time-usage. This is an attempt to see what I can do on my own.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notes in: <a href=\"https://www.notion.so/avery2/QbserveBlocker-883a2b8652eb45b4a0d0b07477871d93\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.notion.so/avery2/QbserveBlocker-883a2b8652eb45b4a0d0b07477871d93</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Gave up once I found a suitable solution using Freedom to schedule blocks on certain applications. I still want a time-based block as well, but this was good enough to the end project.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Future work would use:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://qotoqot.com/qbserve/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Qbserve</a>'s scheduled exports to track time usage</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://freedom.to/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Freedom</a>'s ability to block apps (using Selenium or Beautiful Soup to make it automatic)</li>\n<li>Some system of scripts and mac automator to run the script periodically\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://towardsdatascience.com/how-to-easily-automate-your-python-scripts-on-mac-and-windows-459388c9cc94\" rel=\"nofollow\">possible resource</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
